From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] idle: re-arm the inhibitor once its surface is mapped

Quickshell creates the idle inhibitor as soon as the wl_surface exists,
before the layer surface is mapped. Hyprland counts it as not visible and
only rechecks inhibitors on window or focus events, so Keep awake could
stay ineffective and hypridle still locked the session. Recreate the
inhibitor once, 3 s after start.

Drop when Hyprland rechecks idle inhibitors on layer surface map.
---
 dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
@@ -31,6 +31,20 @@
         Persistent.states.idle.inhibit = root.inhibit;
     }

+    // At startup the inhibitor is created before its layer surface is mapped.
+    // Hyprland then counts it as not visible and only rechecks on window or
+    // focus events, so idle can stay uninhibited. Recreate it once the surface
+    // is mapped.
+    Timer {
+        running: true
+        interval: 3000
+        onTriggered: {
+            if (!root.inhibit) return;
+            root.inhibit = false;
+            Qt.callLater(() => root.inhibit = true);
+        }
+    }
+
     IdleInhibitor {
         id: idleInhibitor
         window: PanelWindow {
--
